<span class="u" data-d="1" data-l="s353S"><span class="u" data-d="5" data-l="s353w1">Lying</span> is when the <span class="u" data-d="5" data-l="s353w9">meanings</span> <span class="u" data-d="6" data-l="s353p8">of</span> one&#x27;s <span class="u" data-d="5" data-l="s353w6">spoken</span> <span class="u" data-d="5" data-l="s353w7">words</span> are <span class="u" data-d="5" data-l="s353w11">understood</span> by the <span class="u" data-d="5" data-l="s353w10">other person</span> involved, and a wrong <span class="u" data-d="5" data-l="s353w5">impression</span> has been given him--<span class="u" data-d="5" data-l="s353w2">purposely</span>, and <span class="u" data-d="6" data-l="s353p3">without</span> any <span class="u" data-d="5" data-l="s353w4">mistaken</span> identity. Next we describe the &quot;four expressions.&quot; 77 The Four Expressions</span>
